Real-time Issue You Should Fixed By AWS CloudWatch 💻

“Your app is running fine… until it isn’t.
Do you want to find out from your users or before your users?”

That’s exactly what Amazon CloudWatch is for: it’s your early warning system in the cloud.

Here’s the step by step guide to configure cloudwatch👇🏻

1️⃣ Enable CloudWatch for your AWS resources
•By default, AWS services like EC2, RDS, Lambda send basic metrics to CloudWatch (CPU, memory, disk, etc.).

2️⃣ Create a CloudWatch Log Group
•Go to CloudWatch Console → Logs → Create Log Group
•Example: /app/logs
